1
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,920
[Episode 25]

2
00:01:49,159 --> 00:01:51,200
So, you're Xing Wu.

3
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:54,200
I'm Qing Ye's father.

4
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:56,560
Ye is coming back home with me tomorrow.

5
00:01:58,519 --> 00:02:00,159
I know.

6
00:02:01,079 --> 00:02:04,959
I need to ask you something.

7
00:02:04,959 --> 00:02:06,640
Sure. What is it?

8
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:08,759
After Ye returns to Beijing,

9
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:11,759
I don't want you two staying in touch.

10
00:02:15,199 --> 00:02:17,560
You shouldn't bring this to me.

11
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:20,439
Who she talks to

12
00:02:20,439 --> 00:02:22,439
is up to her.

13
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:28,240
She is my daughter.

14
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,520
And as a father,

15
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:32,879
I'm not going to let anyone

16
00:02:32,879 --> 00:02:35,759
get in the way of her bright future.

17
00:02:36,919 --> 00:02:40,280
She still holds unrealistic ideas about life.

18
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:43,520
But once she's back in Beijing, she will see

19
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:46,360
that you two
live in completely different worlds.

20
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:48,439
Give it time,

21
00:02:48,439 --> 00:02:50,560
she'll gradually forget about you.

22
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:52,000
Your paths

23
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,378
will never cross again.

24
00:02:57,960 --> 00:02:59,800
Then so be it.

25
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:02,039
As long as she's doing well.

26
00:03:03,439 --> 00:03:05,719
If that's all,

27
00:03:05,719 --> 00:03:07,400
I'll get going.

28
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:17,680
Uncle Qing,

29
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:19,879
After Qing Ye goes back,

30
00:03:19,879 --> 00:03:23,039
please spend more time with her.

31
00:03:23,039 --> 00:03:24,520
She's tough

32
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:26,320
and independent,

33
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:29,280
but she still gets lonely.

34
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:32,960
She needs love from her family.

35
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:07,400
So suddenly.

36
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:09,499
I haven't prepared anything.

37
00:04:10,199 --> 00:04:13,067
I don't even have
a decent goodbye gift for you.

38
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:18,680
Your skill is the best gift.

39
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:21,199
Just give me a nice haircut.

40
00:04:21,199 --> 00:04:23,040
That's more than enough.

41
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:25,000
You're such a sweet talker.

42
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:28,519
When I was young,

43
00:04:28,519 --> 00:04:30,280
I had hair

44
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:32,070
just as nice as yours.

45
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:36,644
You must've been stunning, Auntie.

46
00:04:37,439 --> 00:04:39,040
Stunning? No.

47
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:41,010
Stupid is more like it.

48
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,600
I remember

49
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:44,839
dating a guy

50
00:04:44,839 --> 00:04:46,959
my mother didn't approve of.

51
00:04:46,959 --> 00:04:48,560
Your mom also told me

52
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:50,839
to break up with him,

53
00:04:50,839 --> 00:04:52,199
but I wouldn't listen.

54
00:04:52,199 --> 00:04:54,160
I thought they just

55
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:55,920
didn't get me,

56
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,879
didn't understand love.

57
00:04:57,879 --> 00:04:59,199
In a fit of pique,

58
00:04:59,199 --> 00:05:02,240
I ran away with him.

59
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:03,519
And look at me now.

60
00:05:03,519 --> 00:05:06,205
Your Auntie ended up like this.

61
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:12,439
Full of regrets.

62
00:05:13,399 --> 00:05:15,399
But in life,

63
00:05:15,399 --> 00:05:17,701
there's no undo button.

64
00:05:20,439 --> 00:05:22,839
So don't be stubborn with your dad.

65
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:25,959
Don't let anger

66
00:05:25,959 --> 00:05:28,240
push you onto the wrong path.

67
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:29,920
No parent

68
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:31,160
in this world

69
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:33,321
wants to harm their child.

70
00:05:40,439 --> 00:05:43,120
How do I know what the right path is?

71
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:56,640
Come here,

72
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:58,407
let me take a look.

73
00:06:00,879 --> 00:06:02,600
Okay.

74
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:05,587
Go home with your dad.

75
00:06:06,519 --> 00:06:08,399
Big house,

76
00:06:08,399 --> 00:06:10,720
nice clothes.

77
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:12,639
When you want to study,

78
00:06:12,639 --> 00:06:14,519
study hard.

79
00:06:14,519 --> 00:06:16,160
When you want to have fun,

80
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:18,439
have fun.

81
00:06:18,439 --> 00:06:21,399
Never worry about money again.

82
00:06:21,399 --> 00:06:22,560
That is

83
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:24,044
the right path.

84
00:06:28,519 --> 00:06:29,993
There, all done.

85
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:35,079
Auntie,

86
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:39,253
the hairstyle you did is really beautiful.

87
00:06:41,258 --> 00:06:42,800
Well,

88
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:43,800
my skill

89
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:45,977
is still decent after all.

90
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:50,199
Ye, you look gorgeous.

91
00:09:37,120 --> 00:09:38,720
You awake?

92
00:09:47,519 --> 00:09:49,840
Woke up as soon as you came in.

93
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:53,679
I...

94
00:09:53,679 --> 00:09:56,200
brought you some Tanghulu.

95
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:58,336
I'm leaving tomorrow.

96
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:07,475
Yeah, I heard.

97
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:13,879
It's my last night here.

98
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:16,840
I should do something.

99
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:19,000
I feel like

100
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,138
it would be a pity

101
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:23,840
to just sleep through it.

102
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:32,480
What do you want to do?

103
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:34,200
I'm with you.

104
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:51,080
So much better sitting in the front!

105
00:10:55,039 --> 00:10:57,279
As if you've never sat on my bike before.

106
00:10:57,279 --> 00:10:59,039
Yeah, but never in the front!

107
00:10:59,039 --> 00:11:01,360
It's a completely different feeling.

108
00:11:08,879 --> 00:11:10,840
You know how to fly a plane.

109
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:12,200
You know how to dive.

110
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:14,679
How come you can't handle a little angel?

111
00:11:14,679 --> 00:11:16,440
How do you know that?

112
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,000
Because I'm your brother.

113
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:49,440
In all this time,

114
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:51,275
this is

115
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:53,590
the first time

116
00:11:53,590 --> 00:11:55,240
I've just sat here quietly

117
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:57,459
and looked at the ocean in Zhazhating.

118
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,720
It looks like an oil painting.

119
00:12:01,879 --> 00:12:03,679
Honestly,

120
00:12:03,679 --> 00:12:05,720
it looks more like a circuit board to me.

121
00:12:06,759 --> 00:12:08,399
How so?

122
00:12:08,399 --> 00:12:10,360
Way to kill the mood.

123
00:12:12,759 --> 00:12:14,398
See that spot over there?

124
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:16,640
I used to climb up there

125
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:18,920
all the time when I was little.

126
00:12:19,799 --> 00:12:21,200
So that's like

127
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:23,000
your secret base?

128
00:12:23,679 --> 00:12:24,879
You could say that.

129
00:12:24,879 --> 00:12:26,879
Back then, Xing Guo Dong had a bad temper.

130
00:12:26,879 --> 00:12:28,320
He was always hitting me.

131
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:31,160
So I'd sneak off by myself

132
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:32,840
and climb all the way up there.

133
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:34,759
Wouldn't he find you?

134
00:12:34,759 --> 00:12:35,800
No.

135
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:37,560
Never.

136
00:12:37,560 --> 00:12:40,399
I'd sit up there for the whole day,

137
00:12:40,399 --> 00:12:43,560
watching the sun slowly set in the west,

138
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:45,039
the fishing boats return to the harbor,

139
00:12:45,039 --> 00:12:47,200
and the sky gradually goes dark.

140
00:12:49,399 --> 00:12:50,440
Weren't you scared?

141
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:51,519
I was.

142
00:12:51,519 --> 00:12:53,159
I was terrified as a kid.

143
00:12:53,159 --> 00:12:54,799
You don't notice it while climbing,

144
00:12:54,799 --> 00:12:56,679
but then the wind gets strong,

145
00:12:56,679 --> 00:12:58,000
you're too scared to come down.

146
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,120
Then...

147
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:00,799
Then what? What did you do?

148
00:13:00,799 --> 00:13:02,279
Then I waited.

149
00:13:02,279 --> 00:13:03,720
I'd wait until it got dark,

150
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:05,320
until the lighthouse came on.

151
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:08,240
I thought that light was for me.

152
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:10,399
Suddenly, I wasn't scared anymore.

153
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,759
After that, I'd climbed up there

154
00:13:15,759 --> 00:13:17,360
by myself a lot.

155
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:19,812
I'd count down until the lighthouse lit up.

156
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:24,920
Just like right now.

157
00:13:25,639 --> 00:13:26,799
Five.

158
00:13:26,799 --> 00:13:27,840
Four.

159
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:28,880
Three.

160
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:30,320
Two.

161
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:31,320
One.

162
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:32,840
Light up!

163
00:13:41,919 --> 00:13:43,360
It's late.

164
00:13:43,360 --> 00:13:44,879
Light up!

165
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:55,246
Do you know what a lighthouse is for?

166
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:57,360
A landmark.

167
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:58,600
Exactly.

168
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:00,200
For a ship, a lighthouse is

169
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:02,939
a vital guide showing the way.

170
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:11,000
Qing Ye,

171
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:14,639
you're a born explorer.

172
00:14:14,639 --> 00:14:16,880
It's time to set sail

173
00:14:16,880 --> 00:14:19,277
and conquer your vast ocean.

174
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:28,879
There really is something

175
00:14:28,879 --> 00:14:31,159
about Zhazhating.

176
00:14:33,159 --> 00:14:35,679
The first time I came here,

177
00:14:35,679 --> 00:14:38,039
I was desperate to leave.

178
00:14:38,039 --> 00:14:40,080
The second time,

179
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:42,159
I was desperate to stay.

180
00:14:42,159 --> 00:14:44,080
This time...

181
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:47,879
I was actually thinking

182
00:14:50,879 --> 00:14:53,840
it'd be nice if you could come with me.

183
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:04,360
Once you leave this time,

184
00:15:05,399 --> 00:15:07,360
don't ever come back.

185
00:15:10,279 --> 00:15:12,240
Do you remember

186
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:17,279
what you said to me on New Year's Eve?

187
00:15:22,559 --> 00:15:24,440
I haven't forgotten.

188
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:27,159
You said you'd be

189
00:15:27,159 --> 00:15:29,000
wherever I wanted to be.

190
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:36,161
But with my current grades,

191
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:39,519
there's no way I'll get into

192
00:15:39,519 --> 00:15:42,559
the same university as you,
let alone go abroad.

193
00:15:42,559 --> 00:15:44,399
That's the truth.

194
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:58,759
Xing Wu.

195
00:15:58,759 --> 00:16:00,600
I believe in you.

196
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:03,040
If you want to go,

197
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:05,808
you'll find a hundred different ways
to get there.

198
00:16:07,280 --> 00:16:09,640
If you want to see me again,

199
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:13,437
then walk right up to me on your own.

200
00:16:21,279 --> 00:16:22,840
Okay.

201
00:16:23,759 --> 00:16:25,519
I promise you.

202
00:16:36,039 --> 00:16:38,692
I'm applying to Qingbei University.

203
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:42,340
I'll cut the distance between us

204
00:16:42,340 --> 00:16:44,088
in half.

205
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:46,680
The other half

206
00:16:48,639 --> 00:16:50,395
is on you.

207
00:16:57,679 --> 00:16:59,360
I'll do my best.

208
00:17:01,879 --> 00:17:03,720
Give me your phone.

209
00:17:16,080 --> 00:17:18,574
[Delete contact Qing Ye.]

210
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:25,440
[Are you sure you want to delete "Qing Ye"?]
[Delete / Cancel]

211
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:28,319
I'm deleting our contact information.

212
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:32,279
Until you catch up to me,

213
00:17:34,359 --> 00:17:36,397
we won't be in touch.

214
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:52,298
[Delete contact Xing Wu.]

215
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:04,454
[Xing Wu: are you sure you want to
delete this contact? Cancel / Confirm]

216
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:15,720
Take this as motivation

217
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:17,899
to catch up to me.

218
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:26,486
I hope that the next time we meet,

219
00:18:27,380 --> 00:18:29,965
we'll both be our best selves.

220
00:18:50,160 --> 00:18:51,647
Qing Ye,

221
00:18:53,839 --> 00:18:55,857
just keep moving forward.

222
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:59,463
I'll catch up.

223
00:19:55,160 --> 00:19:56,559
Go back now.

224
00:19:56,559 --> 00:19:58,720
You have work tomorrow.

225
00:20:01,799 --> 00:20:03,920
I'll wait

226
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:05,560
until you're inside.

227
00:20:19,680 --> 00:20:21,759
Will you come tomorrow?

228
00:20:32,559 --> 00:20:34,160
Qing Ye,

229
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:37,200
don't look back.

230
00:22:52,359 --> 00:22:53,440
Never mind.

231
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:56,240
You're more trouble than help.

232
00:22:56,240 --> 00:22:57,400
I've been working

233
00:22:57,400 --> 00:22:59,400
as fast as I can, and this is all I've got.

234
00:22:59,400 --> 00:23:01,319
Qing Ye is leaving tomorrow morning.

235
00:23:01,319 --> 00:23:03,759
How am I supposed to finish in time?

236
00:23:03,759 --> 00:23:06,599
Qing Ye's dad, seriously?

237
00:23:06,599 --> 00:23:08,359
Showing up out of nowhere

238
00:23:08,359 --> 00:23:10,400
and leaving just as suddenly.

239
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:12,668
We weren't prepared at all.

240
00:23:13,759 --> 00:23:16,079
Come to think of it,

241
00:23:16,079 --> 00:23:18,440
Ye never really got to enjoy herself here.

242
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:21,052
Going back with her dad
is probably for the best.

243
00:24:12,640 --> 00:24:14,198
Get in.

244
00:24:16,200 --> 00:24:17,664
Where's your luggage?

245
00:24:18,279 --> 00:24:20,480
It's still early.

246
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:22,200
Dad.

247
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:24,166
Let's go out for breakfast.

248
00:24:45,320 --> 00:24:46,640
Here.

249
00:24:46,640 --> 00:24:49,240
Try our signature seafood noodles.

250
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:51,039
Thank you.

251
00:24:51,039 --> 00:24:52,880
Thank you.

252
00:24:52,880 --> 00:24:54,480
Let me know what you need.

253
00:24:54,480 --> 00:24:57,440
- Ye, take your time.
- Thank you, Auntie Shan Xi.

254
00:25:01,280 --> 00:25:02,840
So the family

255
00:25:02,840 --> 00:25:05,440
you're staying with runs a restaurant.

256
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:06,960
Yes.

257
00:25:06,960 --> 00:25:09,040
They let us

258
00:25:09,040 --> 00:25:10,359
stay in their house.

259
00:25:10,359 --> 00:25:12,776
They're staying elsewhere for now.

260
00:25:14,319 --> 00:25:16,160
No need to wipe it. It's clean.

261
00:25:16,160 --> 00:25:18,200
It's been through the sterilizer.

262
00:25:21,839 --> 00:25:24,400
You used to be so particular about cleanliness.

263
00:25:26,359 --> 00:25:28,000
This place cures germaphobia.

264
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:30,373
Stay long enough
and you'll get used to it, too.

265
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:39,502
See that place across the street
that burned down?

266
00:25:40,559 --> 00:25:42,279
[Xuan Island Barbershop]
I was

267
00:25:42,279 --> 00:25:44,279
living there before.

268
00:25:47,279 --> 00:25:49,799
I came here many years ago.

269
00:25:49,799 --> 00:25:52,400
Didn't expect it to look like this.

270
00:25:52,400 --> 00:25:54,519
At least you're okay.

271
00:25:54,519 --> 00:25:56,599
When I first got here,

272
00:25:57,519 --> 00:26:00,119
Auntie's family cooked with lard.

273
00:26:00,119 --> 00:26:01,740
I couldn't stomach it,

274
00:26:02,319 --> 00:26:03,680
so I went hungry for a day.

275
00:26:03,680 --> 00:26:05,599
My first proper meal

276
00:26:05,599 --> 00:26:07,880
was at this place.

277
00:26:12,519 --> 00:26:14,920
I'm sorry.

278
00:26:14,920 --> 00:26:16,680
I made you suffer.

279
00:26:17,440 --> 00:26:19,641
I thought it was hard back then,

280
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:23,119
but when I look back,

281
00:26:23,119 --> 00:26:25,039
I was quite happy.

282
00:26:29,039 --> 00:26:31,519
Ye, you've grown up.

283
00:26:31,519 --> 00:26:34,799
You're no longer the little girl
in my memory anymore.

284
00:26:34,799 --> 00:26:37,319
Living in an environment like this,

285
00:26:37,319 --> 00:26:38,960
you have to learn

286
00:26:38,960 --> 00:26:40,200
to adapt

287
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:41,440
and find joy in the hard times.

288
00:26:41,440 --> 00:26:43,440
That's how you get through the days.

289
00:26:43,440 --> 00:26:46,039
After coming here,

290
00:26:46,039 --> 00:26:47,880
I realized

291
00:26:48,720 --> 00:26:51,319
how lonely our home in Beijing was

292
00:26:51,319 --> 00:26:53,778
after Mom passed away.

293
00:27:02,400 --> 00:27:03,960
Dad,

294
00:27:04,799 --> 00:27:08,160
when you're starving,

295
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:10,933
would you still worry about
if someone else has enough to eat?

296
00:27:11,759 --> 00:27:13,303
No.

297
00:27:15,440 --> 00:27:17,160
They would.

298
00:27:21,680 --> 00:27:24,315
The same day Xing Wu found out
I don't eat lard,

299
00:27:25,559 --> 00:27:27,959
he switched to vegetable oil.

300
00:27:29,039 --> 00:27:30,759
He changed

301
00:27:31,400 --> 00:27:33,960
the lock on the bathroom shower
in the backyard,

302
00:27:33,960 --> 00:27:35,440
the wardrobe,

303
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:37,559
the air conditioner and light in my bedroom.

304
00:27:37,559 --> 00:27:40,680
Auntie was worried
I wasn't getting enough nutrition,

305
00:27:40,680 --> 00:27:43,485
so she stewed me
pot after pot of pork trotters.

306
00:27:44,359 --> 00:27:46,960
Grandma was afraid I'd lose things again,

307
00:27:46,960 --> 00:27:49,799
so she knitted me all these custom covers

308
00:27:49,799 --> 00:27:51,119
for my pens, my notebooks,

309
00:27:51,119 --> 00:27:52,763
and my laptop.

310
00:27:53,680 --> 00:27:57,200
You might think these are small things,

311
00:27:57,200 --> 00:27:59,079
but each item

312
00:27:59,079 --> 00:28:02,115
stands for their unconditional giving.

313
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:05,281
They treat me like family,

314
00:28:06,240 --> 00:28:08,680
and I treat them like family, too.

315
00:28:10,160 --> 00:28:12,712
So before I leave,

316
00:28:13,720 --> 00:28:16,160
I want to do something for them.

317
00:28:26,079 --> 00:28:28,400
Dad, try it.

318
00:28:28,400 --> 00:28:31,087
The seafood noodles here are really good.

319
00:28:32,279 --> 00:28:33,799
Fine.

320
00:28:46,839 --> 00:28:48,319
Here is 100,000 yuan.

321
00:28:48,319 --> 00:28:49,720
Consider it payment for

322
00:28:49,720 --> 00:28:51,279
taking care of Ye all this time.

323
00:28:51,279 --> 00:28:53,394
Please accept it.

324
00:28:53,394 --> 00:28:56,319
You already paid me for taking care of Ye.

325
00:28:56,319 --> 00:28:58,039
I can't accept this.

326
00:28:58,039 --> 00:29:00,694
Last time I still owed you 20,000 yuan.

327
00:29:01,440 --> 00:29:03,640
And your barbershop needs repairs.

328
00:29:03,640 --> 00:29:04,880
This 100,000 yuan

329
00:29:04,880 --> 00:29:07,359
should make things a little easier for you.

330
00:29:07,359 --> 00:29:09,513
Having money is always better than not.

331
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:14,240
Yes.

332
00:29:14,240 --> 00:29:15,359
You're right.

333
00:29:15,359 --> 00:29:17,519
Who would turn down money?

334
00:29:17,519 --> 00:29:19,160
Fine.

335
00:29:19,160 --> 00:29:20,519
I'll take it.

336
00:29:20,519 --> 00:29:22,931
But I'm writing you an IOU.

337
00:29:37,595 --> 00:29:38,908
[IOU: I, Li Lan Fang,]

338
00:29:41,920 --> 00:29:45,234
Units, tens, hundreds, thousands...

339
00:29:45,234 --> 00:29:46,707
[hereby borrow 100,000 yuan from
Qing Hong Zhi on the Lantern Festival, 2025.]

340
00:29:52,359 --> 00:29:53,440
Here.

341
00:29:53,440 --> 00:29:54,920
Take a look.

342
00:29:58,440 --> 00:30:00,720
I never expected you to pay it back.

343
00:30:00,720 --> 00:30:01,720
I know.

344
00:30:01,720 --> 00:30:03,550
But I'm going to.

345
00:30:04,519 --> 00:30:05,559
I admit,

346
00:30:05,559 --> 00:30:07,160
at first, I was only

347
00:30:07,160 --> 00:30:08,920
looking after Ye for the money.

348
00:30:08,920 --> 00:30:10,440
But after all this time together,

349
00:30:10,440 --> 00:30:13,319
I've come to see her as my own niece.

350
00:30:13,319 --> 00:30:16,160
So thank you, brother-in-law,
for lending me this money.

351
00:30:16,160 --> 00:30:18,519
Even if it's just for Ye's sake,

352
00:30:18,519 --> 00:30:20,799
I must pay this back.

353
00:30:20,799 --> 00:30:22,559
If not in three years, then five.

354
00:30:22,559 --> 00:30:24,400
If not five, then seven.

355
00:30:24,400 --> 00:30:26,039
But

356
00:30:26,039 --> 00:30:28,392
every single yuan will be repaid.

357
00:30:31,839 --> 00:30:34,279
Here, Auntie.

358
00:30:35,880 --> 00:30:37,160
Alright.

359
00:30:37,160 --> 00:30:38,640
Everyone, enough for walking me out.

360
00:30:38,640 --> 00:30:40,279
Or I'll never be able to leave.

361
00:30:40,279 --> 00:30:41,319
Even better.

362
00:30:41,319 --> 00:30:42,519
Then you stay.

363
00:30:42,519 --> 00:30:44,160
I'll cover your food and board.

364
00:30:44,160 --> 00:30:45,880
Stop it.

365
00:30:45,880 --> 00:30:47,240
We can't keep her here anyway.

366
00:30:47,240 --> 00:30:49,519
You're just making us all want to cry.

367
00:30:51,079 --> 00:30:53,079
Ye,

368
00:30:53,079 --> 00:30:54,839
Grandma and I wanted to

369
00:30:54,839 --> 00:30:57,319
to give you something to remember us

370
00:30:57,319 --> 00:30:59,559
when you go back,

371
00:30:59,559 --> 00:31:01,359
but with

372
00:31:01,359 --> 00:31:03,720
Xuan Island gone,

373
00:31:03,720 --> 00:31:07,087
we don't have anything
decent enough to give you.

374
00:31:07,720 --> 00:31:09,920
I wanted to knit you a scarf

375
00:31:09,920 --> 00:31:12,200
to keep you warm on the road,

376
00:31:12,200 --> 00:31:14,400
but I'm old and my hands
don't work like they used to.

377
00:31:14,400 --> 00:31:16,519
I haven't finished it yet.

378
00:31:19,759 --> 00:31:21,880
Grandma.

379
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:24,200
Grandma, you're not old.

380
00:31:24,200 --> 00:31:26,885
You'll live to be 100.

381
00:31:27,519 --> 00:31:30,559
How could I live that long?

382
00:31:30,559 --> 00:31:32,648
You can. Because I said so.

383
00:31:33,240 --> 00:31:36,039
Finish that scarf for me.

384
00:31:36,039 --> 00:31:38,240
I'll come back for it next time.

385
00:31:38,240 --> 00:31:39,519
Okay.

386
00:31:39,519 --> 00:31:41,839
Grandma will be right here waiting for you.

387
00:31:41,839 --> 00:31:44,000
Come back whenever you're free.

388
00:31:44,880 --> 00:31:46,468
Grandma.

389
00:31:48,920 --> 00:31:52,160
I'm going to miss you all so much.

390
00:31:52,160 --> 00:31:55,079
I'll buy you that electric wheelchair

391
00:31:55,079 --> 00:31:57,279
when I come back next time.

392
00:31:58,160 --> 00:31:59,519
Don't you worry about that.

393
00:31:59,519 --> 00:32:02,000
Look, this one works just fine.

394
00:32:02,839 --> 00:32:04,440
When you are back,

395
00:32:04,440 --> 00:32:07,559
take good care of yourself, okay?

396
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:15,640
Ye,

397
00:32:15,640 --> 00:32:17,279
it's time to go.

398
00:32:20,962 --> 00:32:22,319
Go on.

399
00:32:22,319 --> 00:32:24,920
Don't keep your dad waiting.

400
00:32:26,279 --> 00:32:27,839
And don't cry.

401
00:32:27,839 --> 00:32:30,279
You came with a smile, so leave with it, too.

402
00:32:30,279 --> 00:32:31,559
Otherwise, people will think

403
00:32:31,559 --> 00:32:34,519
we bullied you or something.

404
00:32:42,079 --> 00:32:43,319
Okay.

405
00:32:43,319 --> 00:32:45,319
Grandma, I'm leaving now.

406
00:32:45,319 --> 00:32:47,039
Okay.

407
00:32:47,039 --> 00:32:48,799
Alright.

408
00:32:48,799 --> 00:32:51,119
There, there. Good girl.

409
00:32:55,759 --> 00:32:57,920
Auntie Yu Fen,

410
00:32:57,920 --> 00:33:00,160
Auntie Shan Xi,

411
00:33:00,160 --> 00:33:01,839
Auntie,

412
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:04,720
I'm leaving.

413
00:33:07,640 --> 00:33:09,440
Fuzz,

414
00:33:09,440 --> 00:33:11,160
Hu,

415
00:33:13,920 --> 00:33:15,640
see you next time.

416
00:33:16,519 --> 00:33:18,039
Cousin,

417
00:33:18,920 --> 00:33:20,680
are you really leaving?

418
00:33:22,359 --> 00:33:24,920
Can't you just stay?

419
00:33:24,920 --> 00:33:26,400
School starts the day after tomorrow.

420
00:33:26,400 --> 00:33:29,359
What's our study group going to do without you?

421
00:33:29,359 --> 00:33:30,880
Yeah.

422
00:33:30,880 --> 00:33:33,160
I've already talked to Ye Ying Jian.

423
00:33:33,160 --> 00:33:35,279
He'll keep leading your studies.

424
00:33:35,279 --> 00:33:38,360
And I'll send you study materials regularly.

425
00:33:39,880 --> 00:33:41,200
We're a team.

426
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:43,079
Don't let me down.

427
00:33:43,880 --> 00:33:46,799
Thank you all for
taking care of Ye all this time.

428
00:33:46,799 --> 00:33:48,720
Thank you.

429
00:33:48,720 --> 00:33:50,759
Let's go, Ye.

430
00:33:50,759 --> 00:33:53,000
Go on.

431
00:33:53,640 --> 00:33:55,279
Go.

432
00:34:02,799 --> 00:34:05,000
Not going to wait for Xing Wu?

433
00:34:15,880 --> 00:34:17,472
No.

434
00:35:50,039 --> 00:35:51,960
Your phone is ringing.

435
00:35:58,400 --> 00:35:59,635
[Hu]

436
00:36:03,039 --> 00:36:04,559
- Hello?
<i>- Wu.</i>

437
00:36:04,559 --> 00:36:05,679
<i>Qing Ye has left.</i>

438
00:36:05,679 --> 00:36:07,719
<i>Why didn't you come?</i>

439
00:36:28,239 --> 00:36:29,400
When we get back tonight,

440
00:36:29,400 --> 00:36:31,519
we're having dinner with Mr. Meng
and his family.

441
00:36:31,519 --> 00:36:33,519
The house isn't ready yet,

442
00:36:33,519 --> 00:36:36,159
so we'll stay at a hotel tonight.

443
00:36:36,159 --> 00:36:37,880
The hotel is already booked.

444
00:36:37,880 --> 00:36:39,760
Pretty close to home.

445
00:36:40,559 --> 00:36:41,840
I still need to go to the office

446
00:36:41,840 --> 00:36:43,920
and handle some handover stuff.

447
00:36:43,920 --> 00:36:45,000
So for the next couple of days,

448
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:48,039
just rest at the hotel.

449
00:36:48,039 --> 00:36:50,880
It's not easy to start over.

450
00:36:50,880 --> 00:36:52,880
After this, you'll need to come with me

451
00:36:52,880 --> 00:36:55,599
to visit a few uncles and their families.

452
00:36:55,599 --> 00:36:57,239
To maintain relationships,

453
00:36:57,239 --> 00:36:59,116
you have to keep in touch.

454
00:36:59,840 --> 00:37:02,395
Don't dwell on what happened before.

455
00:37:48,119 --> 00:37:49,599
It's getting late.

456
00:37:49,599 --> 00:37:51,519
Let's head straight to the restaurant.

457
00:37:51,519 --> 00:37:53,360
Your Auntie Meng and the others
are already there.

458
00:37:53,360 --> 00:37:55,440
They want to welcome us back.

459
00:37:56,320 --> 00:37:58,280
Do I have to go?

460
00:37:58,280 --> 00:38:00,679
I'd rather go to the hotel and rest.

461
00:38:02,440 --> 00:38:04,800
Dinner first, then rest.

462
00:38:04,800 --> 00:38:06,460
These six months,

463
00:38:07,119 --> 00:38:09,079
I was in Zhazhating

464
00:38:09,079 --> 00:38:11,320
with no one but Auntie's family.

465
00:38:11,320 --> 00:38:14,159
I went to Meng Rui Hang's house.

466
00:38:14,159 --> 00:38:15,486
Back then, I was naive enough

467
00:38:15,486 --> 00:38:17,719
to think that they would help me.

468
00:38:17,719 --> 00:38:19,559
And now

469
00:38:19,559 --> 00:38:21,719
we are all supposed to sit together

470
00:38:21,719 --> 00:38:23,840
happily again

471
00:38:23,840 --> 00:38:26,960
like nothing ever happened?

472
00:38:26,960 --> 00:38:28,159
Funny

473
00:38:28,159 --> 00:38:30,500
how times change.

474
00:38:33,960 --> 00:38:35,800
I know

475
00:38:35,800 --> 00:38:39,119
you're upset about
how the Mengs treated you before.

476
00:38:39,119 --> 00:38:41,360
But that's in the past.

477
00:38:41,360 --> 00:38:43,519
Give them a way to save face.

478
00:38:43,519 --> 00:38:46,097
Our families still have to stay in touch.

479
00:38:51,519 --> 00:38:54,119
You've already made up your mind.

480
00:38:54,119 --> 00:38:56,079
Why even ask me?

481
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:11,880
Isn't it about time they got here?

482
00:39:11,880 --> 00:39:13,079
Here they come!

483
00:39:13,079 --> 00:39:14,119
Mr. Qing.

484
00:39:14,119 --> 00:39:15,599
- Ye!
- Hello, Auntie.

485
00:39:15,599 --> 00:39:16,840
Come here, let me take a look at you.

486
00:39:16,840 --> 00:39:18,879
- Hello, Uncle.
- Good.

487
00:39:19,440 --> 00:39:20,440
You look good.

488
00:39:20,440 --> 00:39:22,719
I'm finally at ease.

489
00:39:22,719 --> 00:39:24,400
Take a seat. Mr. Qing, have a seat.

490
00:39:24,400 --> 00:39:25,400
Qing, sit.

491
00:39:25,400 --> 00:39:27,199
- Good to have you back.
- Sit.

492
00:39:29,360 --> 00:39:30,360
Come on.

493
00:39:30,360 --> 00:39:31,960
Let's all

494
00:39:31,960 --> 00:39:33,760
welcome Mr. Qing and Ye back.

495
00:39:33,760 --> 00:39:36,338
- Cheers. Raise your glasses.
- Serve the food.

496
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:38,320
- Okay.
- Right, right.

497
00:39:38,320 --> 00:39:39,800
- Bring it out.
- Bring it out.

498
00:39:39,800 --> 00:39:41,159
I got a little emotional

499
00:39:41,159 --> 00:39:43,083
just seeing you two.

500
00:39:44,119 --> 00:39:45,360
Qing,

501
00:39:45,360 --> 00:39:47,119
life has its ups and downs.

502
00:39:47,119 --> 00:39:48,760
Luckily, it was just a false alarm.

503
00:39:48,760 --> 00:39:50,159
It hasn't been easy.

504
00:39:50,159 --> 00:39:52,119
This toast is for you.

505
00:39:52,119 --> 00:39:54,119
May your career reach new heights.

506
00:39:54,119 --> 00:39:56,000
Bottoms up.

507
00:39:56,000 --> 00:39:57,800
Let us join in.

508
00:39:59,840 --> 00:40:01,360
During this time,

509
00:40:01,360 --> 00:40:03,599
Ye and I

510
00:40:03,599 --> 00:40:06,519
owe a lot to all of you for your care.

511
00:40:06,519 --> 00:40:07,760
Going forward,

512
00:40:07,760 --> 00:40:09,320
I'll still need

513
00:40:09,320 --> 00:40:10,880
your continued support.

514
00:40:10,880 --> 00:40:13,280
Let's keep working together sincerely.

515
00:40:13,280 --> 00:40:15,719
Here's to everyone.

516
00:40:15,719 --> 00:40:16,719
You're welcome, Mr. Qing.

517
00:40:16,719 --> 00:40:17,920
Come.

518
00:40:17,920 --> 00:40:19,440
Mr. Qing.

519
00:40:24,760 --> 00:40:26,119
Ye,

520
00:40:26,119 --> 00:40:28,654
aren't you going to toast
your uncles and auntie?

521
00:40:30,199 --> 00:40:31,840
All right.

522
00:40:35,039 --> 00:40:36,920
To

523
00:40:36,920 --> 00:40:39,149
uncles and auntie.

524
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:41,800
Alright.

525
00:40:41,800 --> 00:40:43,040
Ye,

526
00:40:43,040 --> 00:40:44,480
sit down.

527
00:40:45,679 --> 00:40:47,010
You look thinner than before,

528
00:40:47,010 --> 00:40:49,559
don't you?

529
00:40:49,559 --> 00:40:51,639
You must have suffered quite a bit

530
00:40:51,639 --> 00:40:54,000
out in the countryside all alone, haven't you?

531
00:40:54,000 --> 00:40:55,159
I was so worried

532
00:40:55,159 --> 00:40:58,199
and really felt for you.

533
00:40:58,199 --> 00:40:59,840
But luckily, you're back now.

534
00:40:59,840 --> 00:41:02,039
Always look forward.

535
00:41:02,039 --> 00:41:03,800
Look forward.

536
00:41:03,800 --> 00:41:05,840
Thank you, Auntie Meng.

537
00:41:05,840 --> 00:41:08,793
Actually,
I had a really good time in Zhazhating.

538
00:41:09,840 --> 00:41:11,280
It was

539
00:41:11,280 --> 00:41:14,079
a very rich experience.

540
00:41:14,079 --> 00:41:15,840
And I made some

541
00:41:15,840 --> 00:41:17,280
really good friends.

542
00:41:17,280 --> 00:41:18,800
<i>In Zhazhating,</i>

543
00:41:18,800 --> 00:41:20,360
<i>Wu has got my back,</i>

544
00:41:20,360 --> 00:41:22,400
<i>and I've got yours.</i>

545
00:41:22,400 --> 00:41:23,519
<i>Aim for Qingbei!</i>

546
00:41:23,519 --> 00:41:26,079
<i>Qing Ye, I believe in you.</i>

547
00:41:28,039 --> 00:41:29,960
<i>Win!</i>

548
00:41:31,840 --> 00:41:32,920
<i>Life has all kinds of flavors.</i>

549
00:41:32,920 --> 00:41:35,280
<i>Face it with a smile.</i>

550
00:41:35,280 --> 00:41:36,920
<i>Draw, meld, pong, win!</i>

551
00:41:36,920 --> 00:41:39,039
<i>Be the big winner!</i>

552
00:41:39,039 --> 00:41:42,199
<i>Every day you live is a day you win.</i>

553
00:41:42,199 --> 00:41:44,199
<i>Living is victory.</i>

554
00:41:44,199 --> 00:41:45,840
<i>Qing Ye,</i>

555
00:41:46,559 --> 00:41:48,928
<i>you're a born explorer.</i>

556
00:41:49,519 --> 00:41:51,760
<i>It's time to set sail</i>

557
00:41:51,760 --> 00:41:53,760
<i>and conquer your vast ocean.</i>

558
00:41:53,760 --> 00:41:56,480
This experience

559
00:41:56,480 --> 00:41:59,079
truly taught me

560
00:41:59,079 --> 00:42:02,599
who is worth cherishing

561
00:42:02,599 --> 00:42:05,578
and what is worth remembering.

562
00:42:07,160 --> 00:42:08,640
Well said.

563
00:42:14,920 --> 00:42:16,360
Mr. Qing, Mr. Meng, we're off now.

564
00:42:16,360 --> 00:42:17,840
- Alright.
- Alright.

565
00:42:18,440 --> 00:42:20,320
The wine was quite good today.

566
00:42:20,320 --> 00:42:22,440
Button up. It's a bit cold.

567
00:42:22,440 --> 00:42:23,599
Thanks for the treat, Meng.

568
00:42:23,599 --> 00:42:24,800
Come visit us at home whenever you're free.

569
00:42:24,800 --> 00:42:26,360
I'll cook your favorite dishes.

570
00:42:26,360 --> 00:42:27,679
